@STATIC_LINKED@
Your rights
-----------

- You may replace any of these DLLs with a modified version of the same library, as long as your
  build stays binary compatible with the one shipped: 64-bit (x64), built with the Microsoft
  Visual C++ compiler against the dynamic C runtime, and the same library version. Qt's modules
  and plugins also use each other's internal interfaces, so replace Qt files with a build of the
  same Qt version and configuration. Copy your build over the file of the same name in the
  installation folder. Lucent does not check signatures or hashes of these DLLs and does nothing
  to prevent their replacement.
- Lucent's terms do not restrict modifying these libraries for your own use, or reverse
  engineering Lucent for debugging such modifications.
- The licence texts are included in this folder:
@LICENCE_TEXTS@

Corresponding source
--------------------

The complete corresponding source of these libraries, as they were built for this version of
Lucent, is the archive

    @SOURCE_PACKAGE@
    (@SOURCE_PACKAGE_SIZE@ bytes, SHA-256 @SOURCE_PACKAGE_SHA256@)

which is published next to Lucent-Setup-@VERSION@-x64.exe, from the same place and for as long as
that installer is offered. It holds, for each library below, the exact upstream source archive,
the build recipe used (the vcpkg port: build script and patches, including the Lucent project's
own changes), the build settings (the vcpkg triplet) and a README that explains how to rebuild
each library and replace its DLL. You do not need Lucent's own source code (MIT License) to
rebuild or replace these libraries; it is published at @HOMEPAGE@.

The libraries were built from the upstream source archives listed below, with the build recipe
(build script and patches) of the vcpkg port named for each. vcpkg verifies every archive against
the SHA-512 value shown. A recipe is identified by the git tree hash of its port folder in the
vcpkg registry (https://github.com/microsoft/vcpkg) and, when the registry commit Lucent builds
against (@VCPKG_BASELINE@) holds exactly that tree, by a link to the port folder at that commit.
A port that Lucent overlays (vcpkg's recipe with Lucent's build changes) is installed with Lucent
in the folder named for it (licenses\<port>\recipe): its patches named lucent-*.patch are the
Lucent project's only changes to the library's source, each described in the patch and in the
recipe's portfile.cmake. Every other library is built without changes by the Lucent project. The
same information is available in machine-readable form in Lucent.spdx.json (SPDX 2.3), and in
MANIFEST.json inside the archive above.

